<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Venetian Morea</h1><p class="st-meta">1688 CE – 1715 CE · capital Nauplia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Peloponnese under Venice after Morosini's conquest in 1685-1687, a brief reform-minded colony that collapsed in the Ottoman reconquest of 1715.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morean-war">Morean War</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a>, the Venetian commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-morosini">Francesco Morosini</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> between 1685 and 1687; during his campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> a Venetian shell exploded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthenon">Parthenon</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> in 1699 confirmed Venetian possession of the Morea as the Kingdom of the Morea.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> divided the peninsula into four provinces under a provveditore generale at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>, carried out a detailed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a> and land register, and settled colonists to revive a depopulated, war-damaged land. It favoured the Catholic church, which irritated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> majority, and built the great fortress of Palamidi above Nauplia in 1711-1714.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> attacked in 1715 and took the whole <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a> within a few months, helped by weak garrisons and the indifference of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-passarowitz">Treaty of Passarowitz</a> in 1718 confirmed the Ottoman reconquest.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/venetian-morea.jpg" alt="Venetian Morea" width="320" height="210"><figcaption>Image: Wit, Frederik de · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peloponnesus,_Presently_the_Kingdom_of_Morea,_Clearly_Divided_into_All_Its_Provinces,_Both_Contemporary_and_Ancient,_and_to_which_is_Added_the_Islands_of_Cefalonia,_Zante,_Cerigo,_and_St._Maura_WDL373.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1688 CE – 1715 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nauplia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Francesco Morosini</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity, Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek, Venetian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of the Morea, Regno di Morea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1702&amp;focus=venetian-morea" aria-label="Venetian Morea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5250 826 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Venetian Morea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5570 1082L5293 831M5570 1082L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5293 831h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5570 1082h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5570 1082h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nauplia. <a href="/atlas?year=1702&amp;focus=venetian-morea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

